@@ -0,0 +1,167 @@
+# JeRyu Web Forge
+
+JeRyu Web Forge is the browser surface for the JeRyu control plane. It is not a thin clone of GitHub or GitLab; it is a full repository forge that keeps the useful primitives of both products while removing navigation friction and exposing JeRyu's live agent/control-plane state directly.
+
+## Goals
+
+- See every repository across local, GitLab, GitHub, mirrors, and repo families.
+- Create, import, fork, mirror, archive, and delete repositories with safety previews.
+- Browse code, commits, branches, tags, blame, history, and artifacts.
+- Render `README.md` and other Markdown to sanitized HTML.
+- Review merge requests with virtualized diffs, exact-SHA approvals, comments, checks, evidence capsules, and safe merge buttons.
+- Manage issues, boards, labels, milestones, releases, packages, webhooks, CI variables, secrets, branch protections, members, and automation settings.
+- Watch all underlying activity live through a replayable WebSocket.
+
+## Architecture
+
+```text
+apps/web/                 Vite + React + TypeScript SPA
+  src/api/                typed REST client and contract validation
+  src/realtime/           websocket client, replay, reducers
+  src/pages/              dashboard, repos, repo, review, settings
+  src/components/         README, markdown, actions, diff, forms
+
+src/web/                  Axum browser backend-for-frontend
+  router.rs               /api/web, /ws/activity, static SPA mount
+  rest/                   typed REST handlers
+  ws.rs                   browser websocket protocol
+  activity.rs             bounded replay/fanout hub
+  markdown.rs             pulldown-cmark + ammonia renderer
+  auth.rs                 session/RBAC extraction boundary
+
+src/api/                  shared DTOs, events, snapshots, generated TS contracts
+src/git_host/             GitHub/GitLab/local provider adapter surface
+db/migrations/            web read-model, cache, audit, preference tables
+```
+
+## HTTP routes
+
+| Route | Purpose |
+|---|---|
+| `GET /api/web/dashboard` | Global attention dashboard |
+| `GET /api/web/repos` | List all repositories |
+| `POST /api/web/repos` | Create/import/mirror repository |
+| `GET /api/web/repos/:owner/:repo` | Repository overview |
+| `GET /api/web/repos/:owner/:repo/readme` | Render README Markdown to sanitized HTML |
+| `GET /api/web/repos/:owner/:repo/tree/:ref` | Code tree |
+| `GET /api/web/repos/:owner/:repo/blob/:ref` | File/blob content |
+| `GET /api/web/repos/:owner/:repo/merge-requests` | Merge request list |
+| `GET /api/web/repos/:owner/:repo/merge-requests/:iid` | Review room detail |
+| `POST /api/web/repos/:owner/:repo/merge-requests/:iid/approve` | Exact-SHA approval |
+| `POST /api/web/repos/:owner/:repo/merge-requests/:iid/merge` | Safe merge |
+| `GET/PATCH /api/web/repos/:owner/:repo/settings` | Repository settings |
+| `POST /api/web/actions/preview` | Preview a mutation |
+| `POST /api/web/actions/execute` | Execute a previewed mutation |
+| `GET /ws/activity` | Replayable activity WebSocket |
+
+## WebSocket protocol
+
+The browser hydrates a page with REST and subscribes to activity topics over `/ws/activity`. Events are monotonic and replayable. The client stores `lastSeq`; reconnect requests replay from `lastSeq + 1`. If the replay window has expired, the server sends a gap frame and the client refetches affected read models.
+
+Topics:
+
+- `global.activity`
+- `repo:{repo_id}`
+- `repo:{repo_id}:code`
+- `repo:{repo_id}:mrs`
+- `repo:{repo_id}:issues`
+- `repo:{repo_id}:ci`
+- `repo:{repo_id}:agents`
+- `repo:{repo_id}:settings`
+- `user:{user_id}:notifications`
+- `admin:audit`
+
+## README rendering
+
+Server rendering is mandatory for trustworthy README display. The renderer:
+
+1. reads Markdown from the provider blob surface;
+2. renders GitHub-flavored Markdown with `pulldown-cmark`;
+3. sanitizes HTML with `ammonia`;
+4. extracts a table of contents;
+5. rewrites relative links/images through blob/raw routes;
+6. caches by repo/ref/path/source hash;
+7. emits a `readme.rendered` event.
+
+## Mutation contract
+
+Every mutating action follows a preview/execute/audit/stream lifecycle.
+
+1. Client sends `POST /api/web/actions/preview` or a domain preview endpoint.
+2. Server returns risk, affected entities, permission checks, exact SHA, dry-run plan, and rollback story.
+3. Client confirms when risk is medium/high/destructive.
+4. Client sends execute request with an idempotency key.
+5. Server writes audit rows, performs mutation, emits WebSocket events, and returns the final receipt.
+
+## Validation
+
+```bash
+cargo check -p jeryu --message-format=json
+cargo nextest run -p jeryu -- web api::repository api::repo_browser api::merge_request
+npm run typecheck
+npm run test
+npm run build
+npm run test:e2e
+```
+
+## Rollout order
+
+1. Move the existing UX QA stub to `apps/ux-qa` and make `apps/web` a real Vite app.
+2. Add `src/web` BFF routes, static serving, and WebSocket replay hub.
+3. Add repository list/detail/readme/code browser surfaces.
+4. Extend `GitHost` with full repository/tree/blob/settings/review capabilities.
+5. Add merge request review room with exact-SHA approve/merge.
+6. Add settings matrix, audit log, and action preview/execute.
+7. Add issues/boards/releases/packages/secrets/webhooks.
+8. Harden auth, RBAC, CSRF, contract generation, accessibility, and performance budgets.
